# Build artifacts. Everything kama generates lands under one root — see `out` in kama.json.
out/

# Resolved dependencies. Reproducible from kama.json + kama.lock, so they are not committed.
.kama/

# Per-machine manifest override (deep-merges over kama.json). Yours, not the project's.
kama.local.json

# Throwaway prototypes and probes (the design spike measures things here).
.scratch/

# Each example is its own repository, cloned here by kind by those who want it: a game as `examples/games/<name>`
# (kyoten-example-fps, kyoten-example-vr, …). Ignored so the engine stays small for everyone who only wants the engine.
# A new kind of example (a simulation, a graphics sample) gets its own folder under examples/ and its own line. See
# README.md.
examples/games/

# The pinned kama compiler: a copy kyoten builds with, made from a clean clone of kama at the commit .kama-version
# names (AGENTS.kyoten.md § Build). Each machine makes its own; ../kama is rebuilt as it develops.
.kama-pin/
